35
00:02:50,570 --> 00:02:51,836
Call the police.

36
00:03:07,621 --> 00:03:09,253
How may I help you, sir?

37
00:03:09,289 --> 00:03:10,889
You in charge here?

38
00:03:10,924 --> 00:03:13,391
I'm Martin Washburn,
one of the society's elders.

39
00:03:13,426 --> 00:03:14,860
Joshua Bradbury is our leader.

40
00:03:14,895 --> 00:03:17,229
Yeah? Well, where is he?

41
00:03:17,264 --> 00:03:18,497
Mr. Bradbury's busy.

42
00:03:18,532 --> 00:03:20,065
We'll make an appointment.

43
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:24,469
Like hell. Get out of my way.
- It's all right, Martin.

44
00:03:27,007 --> 00:03:30,642
Joshua will see the gentleman.

45
00:03:30,678 --> 00:03:32,611
Of course.

46
00:03:32,646 --> 00:03:34,212
This way, sir.

47
00:03:44,591 --> 00:03:47,960
Mr. Austin, this is our
founder Joshua Bradbury.

48
00:03:47,995 --> 00:03:49,861
I want my son.

49
00:03:51,798 --> 00:03:55,166
You sound very
angry, Mr. Austin.

50
00:03:55,201 --> 00:03:56,601
You're damn right I am.

51
00:03:56,637 --> 00:03:57,936
You're holding my son.

52
00:03:57,971 --> 00:04:01,372
No, no, we don't hold anyone.

53
00:04:01,408 --> 00:04:04,843
Your son came here
because he found your world,

54
00:04:04,878 --> 00:04:09,013
the outside world,
corrupt, decayed.

55
00:04:09,048 --> 00:04:11,549
We're the future, Mr. Austin.

56
00:04:11,584 --> 00:04:13,463
I don't give a
damn what you are.

57
00:04:13,487 --> 00:04:15,620
You can't keep me from my son.

58
00:04:15,655 --> 00:04:17,088
Of course not.

59
00:04:17,124 --> 00:04:21,225
We wouldn't think of holding
anyone against his will.

60
00:04:25,699 --> 00:04:29,500
Nobody is trying to keep
anybody from anyone.

61
00:04:35,375 --> 00:04:37,520
You wish to speak to me, Joshua?

62
00:04:37,544 --> 00:04:40,912
My God, Dennis,
what's happened to you?

63
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:47,152
Dennis, answer your father.

64
00:04:47,187 --> 00:04:50,789
You shouldn't have come here.

65
00:04:50,824 --> 00:04:52,057
What else could I do?

66
00:04:52,092 --> 00:04:53,425
You disappeared from school.

67
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:57,595
Your friends told me
you went off to join a cult.

68
00:04:57,630 --> 00:04:59,831
We are the future.
The future is now.

69
00:04:59,866 --> 00:05:02,567
We are the future.
What is this crap?

70
00:05:02,602 --> 00:05:05,637
Dennis, I'm your father.

71
00:05:05,672 --> 00:05:08,106
I love you.

72
00:05:08,142 --> 00:05:09,574
I'm taking you home.

73
00:05:10,677 --> 00:05:12,677
This is my home.

74
00:05:12,712 --> 00:05:14,612
This is my family.

75
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:16,781
What have you done to my son?

76
00:05:16,816 --> 00:05:19,985
Mr. Austin, you
offered the past.

77
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:23,922
What we've done is to
give Dennis an opportunity...

78
00:05:23,957 --> 00:05:26,024
An opportunity for perspective

79
00:05:26,059 --> 00:05:27,458
to see into the mind's eye...

80
00:05:27,494 --> 00:05:29,527
A very clear and
pure perspective

81
00:05:29,562 --> 00:05:31,797
into the very life of things.

82
00:05:31,832 --> 00:05:33,264
The future, Mr. Austin.

83
00:05:33,299 --> 00:05:36,201
Dennis has chosen the future.

84
00:05:36,236 --> 00:05:40,405
It's a very important and
happy time for all of us.

85
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:43,341
But this is private property,

86
00:05:43,377 --> 00:05:45,543
and I must ask you to leave.

87
00:05:45,579 --> 00:05:47,845
Not without my son!

88
00:05:47,881 --> 00:05:49,459
Dennis, what's the
matter with you?!

89
00:05:49,483 --> 00:05:51,683
What the hell is
going on around here?

90
00:05:51,718 --> 00:05:52,829
Damn you, I'll
take your head off

91
00:05:52,853 --> 00:05:54,053
before I let you keep my boy!

92
00:05:54,087 --> 00:05:55,965
What's the problem here?

93
00:05:55,989 --> 00:05:57,088
I'm William Austin.

94
00:05:57,123 --> 00:05:58,356
This is my son Dennis.

95
00:05:58,391 --> 00:05:59,825
And these, these people...

96
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:01,093
They're holding him.

97
00:06:01,128 --> 00:06:02,961
That true?

98
00:06:02,996 --> 00:06:06,731
Is that true, Dennis?

99
00:06:06,767 --> 00:06:09,044
This man is not my father.

100
00:06:09,068 --> 00:06:10,735
This is my home.

101
00:06:10,770 --> 00:06:12,237
This is my family.

102
00:06:12,272 --> 00:06:15,573
And this man is trespassing.

103
00:06:15,609 --> 00:06:18,577
He threatened my life, and
I want to file a complaint.

104
00:06:18,612 --> 00:06:20,879
File a complaint?
What, against me?

105
00:06:20,914 --> 00:06:24,048
He kidnapped my son!

106
00:06:24,083 --> 00:06:25,995
Do you want to leave?

107
00:06:26,019 --> 00:06:27,318
This is my home.

108
00:06:27,353 --> 00:06:28,664
That's it, Mr. Austin, let's go.

109
00:06:28,688 --> 00:06:31,389
No! I'll kill you!

110
00:06:31,425 --> 00:06:32,468
I'll kill you!

111
00:06:32,492 --> 00:06:33,803
Come on. No!

112
00:06:33,827 --> 00:06:37,161
Leave me alone!

113
00:06:44,538 --> 00:06:47,471
Are you people nuts?

114
00:06:47,507 --> 00:06:49,919
This lunatic Bradbury
has kidnapped my son,

115
00:06:49,943 --> 00:06:51,621
and you're putting me in jail.

116
00:06:51,645 --> 00:06:54,512
Mr. Austin, your son's
an adult with rights.

117
00:06:54,548 --> 00:06:55,947
Just like you and me.

118
00:06:55,982 --> 00:06:57,849
And you have no right
to threaten Mr. Bradbury.

119
00:06:57,884 --> 00:06:59,283
This cult has taken my son,

120
00:06:59,319 --> 00:07:01,331
and that man Bradbury
is the head of it.

121
00:07:01,355 --> 00:07:04,588
It's some kind of a religion,
and it's not against the law.

122
00:07:04,624 --> 00:07:06,558
Now please, empty your pockets.

123
00:07:09,096 --> 00:07:12,464
Booking desk.

124
00:07:12,499 --> 00:07:15,233
Yes.

125
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:17,168
I see. Fine.

126
00:07:19,139 --> 00:07:20,905
You lucked out.

127
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:23,741
Joshua Bradbury has decided
to withdraw his complaint.

128
00:07:23,776 --> 00:07:27,445
You're free to go.

129
00:07:27,481 --> 00:07:30,147
Mr. Austin, you've done
what you could for your boy.

130
00:07:30,183 --> 00:07:32,417
Go back to Chicago.

131
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:36,221
I'm not going anywhere
without my son.

132
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:22,734
It's almost 11:00.

133
00:08:22,769 --> 00:08:24,435
Time for Joshua's tea.

134
00:08:24,471 --> 00:08:27,072
Oh?

135
00:08:27,107 --> 00:08:29,140
Anna, you all right?

136
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:30,608
I'm fine.

137
00:08:30,643 --> 00:08:33,311
My baby is blessed.

138
00:08:33,347 --> 00:08:36,313
I'll be back in a minute to
help you finish your work.

139
00:08:36,349 --> 00:08:38,016
You look tired.

140
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:10,348
No.

141
00:09:28,535 --> 00:09:31,802
Oh, my God!

142
00:09:43,283 --> 00:09:46,084
I'd love to have taken
that jackass's head off,

143
00:09:46,119 --> 00:09:47,418
but this is insane.

144
00:09:47,454 --> 00:09:49,621
Dennis couldn't
have seen me kill him.

145
00:09:49,656 --> 00:09:52,201
What your son actually said was,

146
00:09:52,225 --> 00:09:54,370
he saw you fleeing
the scene of the crime.

147
00:09:54,394 --> 00:09:56,127
But I wasn't there.

148
00:09:56,163 --> 00:09:59,964
I mean, this-this
can't be happening.

149
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:03,901
You told the police you went to
meet a man who never showed up?

150
00:10:03,936 --> 00:10:05,904
I did. At the time
of the murder?

151
00:10:05,939 --> 00:10:08,673
Yes, I think so.

152
00:10:10,309 --> 00:10:12,043
Well, this is all my fault.

153
00:10:12,079 --> 00:10:15,947
See, Dennis... Dennis
has always been

154
00:10:15,982 --> 00:10:18,350
a fragile boy, and
when his mother

155
00:10:18,385 --> 00:10:21,352
passed away last
year, he was devastated.

156
00:10:21,387 --> 00:10:24,022
Happened so
fast, I was out of it.

157
00:10:24,057 --> 00:10:26,490
I mean, I... I didn't
recognize his pain.

158
00:10:26,526 --> 00:10:28,492
I wasn't any help to him at all.

159
00:10:28,528 --> 00:10:29,961
I just told him time would heal,

160
00:10:29,996 --> 00:10:31,474
and I shipped
him back to school.

161
00:10:31,498 --> 00:10:34,231
Now with his mother gone

162
00:10:34,267 --> 00:10:37,135
and me... me acting
like I didn't give a damn,

163
00:10:37,170 --> 00:10:40,672
well, no wonder that
cult was able to grab him.

164
00:10:40,707 --> 00:10:43,274
You think the cult got your son

165
00:10:43,310 --> 00:10:46,044
to accuse you of murder?

166
00:10:46,079 --> 00:10:47,578
Well, certainly.

167
00:10:47,613 --> 00:10:49,947
They already got him
to sign over his trust fund

168
00:10:49,982 --> 00:10:51,048
and his inheritance.

169
00:10:51,084 --> 00:10:54,518
It was $400,000.

170
00:10:56,256 --> 00:10:58,367
Look, they tell me you're
the best lawyer in Atlanta.

171
00:10:58,391 --> 00:10:59,524
Is that so?

172
00:10:59,559 --> 00:11:03,962
I don't know that
I'm the one to ask.

173
00:11:03,997 --> 00:11:06,731
Please, you talk to Dennis.

174
00:11:06,766 --> 00:11:10,101
Maybe you can get
him to clear this up.

175
00:11:10,136 --> 00:11:15,473
What if I talk to him,
and he sticks to his story?

176
00:11:17,110 --> 00:11:19,177
I don't know.

177
00:11:19,212 --> 00:11:20,745
But if I go to prison,

178
00:11:20,780 --> 00:11:23,614
Dennis is going to be lost
to those people forever.

179
00:11:30,924 --> 00:11:33,691
Dennis? Dennis Austin?

180
00:11:33,726 --> 00:11:35,260
Uh, I'm Ben Matlock.

181
00:11:35,295 --> 00:11:36,972
I'll be representing
your father.

182
00:11:36,996 --> 00:11:38,696
I'm Martin Washburn,

183
00:11:38,731 --> 00:11:40,665
the attorney for the
Future Now Society.

184
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:42,667
Dennis has nothing to
say to you, Mr. Matlock.

185
00:11:42,702 --> 00:11:45,670
Uh, Dennis, can't
you speak for yourself?

186
00:11:45,705 --> 00:11:49,374
Joshua Bradbury was
the hope for the future,

187
00:11:49,409 --> 00:11:52,610
and this evil man,
William Austin, killed him.

188
00:11:52,645 --> 00:11:54,913
He denies that.

189
00:11:54,948 --> 00:11:57,682
How can you talk that
way about your own father?

190
00:11:57,717 --> 00:11:58,916
He's not my father.

191
00:11:58,951 --> 00:12:01,219
He's a liar and a subversive,

192
00:12:01,254 --> 00:12:03,174
and I never want
to see him again.

193
00:12:12,766 --> 00:12:15,166
<i>Come on in.</i>

194
00:12:15,201 --> 00:12:17,635
Mrs. Carter?

195
00:12:17,670 --> 00:12:21,272
Mrs. Carter, I know
it's difficult, but...

196
00:12:21,308 --> 00:12:23,308
Try not to worry, Mrs. Carter.

197
00:12:23,343 --> 00:12:26,511
If your daughter's in
the Moonies, I'll find her.

198
00:12:26,546 --> 00:12:28,379
No, I'll call you.

199
00:12:28,415 --> 00:12:31,048
Okay, bye.

200
00:12:31,084 --> 00:12:32,783
You're Ben Matlock.

201
00:12:32,819 --> 00:12:34,219
Yes, sir.

202
00:12:34,254 --> 00:12:36,121
You make the papers.

203
00:12:36,156 --> 00:12:37,722
Well, sometimes, I guess.

204
00:12:37,757 --> 00:12:39,469
Did you track down
all these folks?

205
00:12:39,493 --> 00:12:40,925
Yeah, most of them.

206
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:43,828
They're the ones I tracked down,
I deprogrammed successfully.

207
00:12:43,863 --> 00:12:45,196
I've heard.

208
00:12:45,232 --> 00:12:48,433
Ah... What's on your mind?

209
00:12:48,468 --> 00:12:54,939
Um, well, I... I have a problem.

210
00:12:54,974 --> 00:12:58,409
My client William Austin

211
00:12:58,444 --> 00:13:01,913
has been accused of
murdering Joshua Bradbury.

212
00:13:01,948 --> 00:13:03,581
Oh, I read about it.

213
00:13:03,616 --> 00:13:05,816
Somebody should have
done that a long time ago.

214
00:13:09,155 --> 00:13:11,555
The Future Now Society.

215
00:13:11,591 --> 00:13:14,425
A very rich cult.

216
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:18,095
They make all their new
members sign over all their assets.

217
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:21,065
Bank accounts, property,
even life insurance policies.

218
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:23,868
And they're very
good at investments.

219
00:13:25,605 --> 00:13:28,973
Well, what do the people who
join this society get out of it?

220
00:13:29,008 --> 00:13:34,778
In return for their money
and absolute obedience,

221
00:13:34,814 --> 00:13:37,582
cults provide their
victims with the illusion

222
00:13:37,617 --> 00:13:40,784
that they're on the side of
good, fighting against evil,

223
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:43,020
that their leader is
greater than God.

224
00:13:44,758 --> 00:13:46,323
Oh.

225
00:13:46,359 --> 00:13:49,660
Con games dressed
up to look like religion.

226
00:13:52,265 --> 00:13:56,767
My client's son Dennis

227
00:13:56,802 --> 00:13:58,836
told the police
he saw his father

228
00:13:58,872 --> 00:14:00,471
fleeing the scene of the crime.

229
00:14:00,506 --> 00:14:03,341
Dennis is a cult member, is he?

230
00:14:03,376 --> 00:14:04,820
Yeah, he's been a
member for two months.

231
00:14:04,844 --> 00:14:06,844
I-I-I think he's lying.

232
00:14:06,879 --> 00:14:08,157
Oh, I doubt that.

233
00:14:08,181 --> 00:14:11,549
Well, I'm certain
my client's innocent.

234
00:14:11,584 --> 00:14:14,885
Cults dwell on the
purity of their world

235
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:17,521
and the corruption and
deceit of everyone else.

236
00:14:17,557 --> 00:14:19,490
They'd never ask the boy to lie.

237
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:23,994
Well, how could Dennis
say he saw his father?

238
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:28,533
What do you know about
brainwashing, Mr. Matlock?

239
00:14:28,568 --> 00:14:31,735
Not much.

240
00:14:31,771 --> 00:14:33,204
Let me put it this way.

241
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:34,672
Given the right circumstances,

242
00:14:34,708 --> 00:14:37,875
you or I could be
programmed to see...

243
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:41,045
that phone and
think it was a snake,

244
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:44,949
or a monster, or God.

245
00:14:44,984 --> 00:14:48,353
That's hard to believe.

246
00:14:48,388 --> 00:14:49,553
It's true.

247
00:14:49,589 --> 00:14:50,955
Cults control minds.

248
00:14:50,990 --> 00:14:52,856
That's how they work.

249
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:55,326
It's what they do.

250
00:14:55,361 --> 00:14:57,094
And I undo.

251
00:14:57,130 --> 00:15:00,164
Well, um, thank you

252
00:15:00,199 --> 00:15:02,500
and I'll be leaving. I may...

253
00:15:02,535 --> 00:15:03,835
may be coming back.

254
00:15:03,870 --> 00:15:05,003
Do it.

255
00:15:05,038 --> 00:15:06,703
Thanks.

256
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:08,606
Mm-hmm.

257
00:15:11,377 --> 00:15:14,445
Pretty impressive place
for a religious organization

258
00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:17,148
that sends kids out in
the street to sell flowers.

259
00:15:17,183 --> 00:15:18,883
Yeah, well...

260
00:15:18,918 --> 00:15:21,819
the flowers are just
what the public sees.

261
00:15:21,855 --> 00:15:25,656
The money these poor
people turn over to this cult

262
00:15:25,691 --> 00:15:29,693
has given Mr. Bradbury
two mansions,

263
00:15:29,729 --> 00:15:32,963
a fleet of cars, boats,

264
00:15:32,998 --> 00:15:36,534
no telling how many
secret bank accounts.

265
00:15:36,569 --> 00:15:37,802
Well, now that he's dead,

266
00:15:37,837 --> 00:15:40,237
maybe the Future Now
Society will fall apart.

267
00:15:40,273 --> 00:15:42,407
Well, now, here,

268
00:15:42,442 --> 00:15:44,909
they've got elders
who've already taken over.

269
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:47,189
You think one of them
killed Joshua Bradbury?

270
00:15:47,213 --> 00:15:49,947
They were all there when
William Austin threatened him

271
00:15:49,982 --> 00:15:51,093
and tried to strangle him.

272
00:15:51,117 --> 00:15:53,128
I guarantee you, one of
them made the phone call,

273
00:15:53,152 --> 00:15:56,321
left him without an alibi. Mm.

274
00:15:56,356 --> 00:15:58,434
Mr. Matlock. Miss Thomas.

275
00:15:58,458 --> 00:16:00,369
I'm Thomas Oldham,
one of the elders.

276
00:16:00,393 --> 00:16:03,427
I believe you've
met Mr. Washburn.

277
00:16:03,462 --> 00:16:04,573
Quite a place you've got here.

278
00:16:04,597 --> 00:16:06,497
Let's get this over
with, Mr. Matlock.

279
00:16:06,532 --> 00:16:09,267
One of you can see our
new leader, Ezra Smith.

280
00:16:09,302 --> 00:16:11,336
The other can
see Joshua's study.

281
00:16:13,273 --> 00:16:16,841
Well, what, do we flip?

282
00:16:16,876 --> 00:16:18,575
I'll take the study.

283
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:23,047
Mr. Smith is downstairs.
The study is upstairs.

284
00:16:31,591 --> 00:16:34,958
Now, the police say

285
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:38,429
the killer entered
through these, uh,

286
00:16:38,464 --> 00:16:40,042
French doors and
left the same way,

287
00:16:40,066 --> 00:16:42,934
with, uh, Dennis following him.

288
00:16:42,969 --> 00:16:44,268
That's right.

289
00:16:44,303 --> 00:16:46,670
And at a certain point,

290
00:16:46,705 --> 00:16:49,173
the killer fell, and
that's when Dennis saw

291
00:16:49,209 --> 00:16:50,641
that it was his father.

292
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:51,842
Yes.

293
00:16:51,877 --> 00:16:52,921
Are you finished, Mr. Matlock?

294
00:16:52,945 --> 00:16:54,745
No.

295
00:16:58,518 --> 00:17:01,118
Now, as I understand it,

296
00:17:01,154 --> 00:17:07,558
uh, Dennis Austin was
bringing tea to Mr. Bradbury

297
00:17:07,593 --> 00:17:10,161
when he heard the shot.

298
00:17:10,196 --> 00:17:11,529
That's a coincidence.

299
00:17:11,564 --> 00:17:13,542
Here comes young
Dennis, bringing tea

300
00:17:13,566 --> 00:17:15,232
at the exact moment

301
00:17:15,267 --> 00:17:18,369
his father's supposed
to be shooting this fella.

302
00:17:18,405 --> 00:17:24,175
Yes, but Dennis always
brought tea to Joshua at that time.

303
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:26,244
Oh, I see.

304
00:17:26,279 --> 00:17:27,512
Huh.

305
00:17:27,547 --> 00:17:28,613
Every night?

306
00:17:28,648 --> 00:17:30,247
At 11:00.

307
00:17:30,282 --> 00:17:31,682
Hmm.

308
00:17:31,718 --> 00:17:37,154
Um, what, uh, what were you
two gentlemen doing when, uh...

309
00:17:37,190 --> 00:17:39,557
Joshua was murdered?

310
00:17:39,592 --> 00:17:41,659
This is outrageous, Mr. Matlock.

311
00:17:41,694 --> 00:17:46,130
Um, Martin's a very
volatile man, Mr. Matlock,

312
00:17:46,165 --> 00:17:48,966
and was totally
dedicated to Joshua.

313
00:17:49,002 --> 00:17:51,180
His loss has made him angry.

314
00:17:51,204 --> 00:17:53,449
Now, to answer your question,

315
00:17:53,473 --> 00:17:56,974
Martin, Ezra, and
I emulated Joshua.

316
00:17:57,009 --> 00:18:01,779
From dinner until 11:00,
we each meditated privately.

317
00:18:01,815 --> 00:18:03,848
Oh, I see.

318
00:18:03,883 --> 00:18:05,516
Uh-huh.

319
00:18:05,552 --> 00:18:06,851
Well, one more thing.

320
00:18:06,886 --> 00:18:09,153
Um, um, you say that, um,

321
00:18:09,188 --> 00:18:12,356
Mr. Smith is now your
leader, your new leader.

322
00:18:12,391 --> 00:18:15,059
When was the election?

323
00:18:15,094 --> 00:18:18,195
Joshua named me his
successor in his will, Miss Thomas.

324
00:18:18,230 --> 00:18:20,731
Mr. Bradbury expected to die?

325
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:23,166
We all die, Miss Thomas.

326
00:18:23,202 --> 00:18:26,770
But that's not
what you're asking.

327
00:18:26,805 --> 00:18:29,440
Joshua was realistic.

328
00:18:29,475 --> 00:18:33,410
He found it quite possible
he might meet a violent end.

329
00:18:33,446 --> 00:18:34,645
You see,

330
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:38,649
people misunderstand
our society, our goals

331
00:18:38,684 --> 00:18:41,485
and the devotion
of our followers.

332
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:43,688
Like Dennis Austin.

333
00:18:43,723 --> 00:18:49,593
Yes. When Dennis first came
here, he was confused, lost.

334
00:18:49,628 --> 00:18:54,364
We gave him love, a
home and a purpose in life.

335
00:18:55,568 --> 00:18:58,536
Do any of those things
sound evil to you?

336
00:18:58,571 --> 00:19:01,638
Of course not,
but... Miss Thomas,

337
00:19:01,674 --> 00:19:03,808
you're obviously a
resourceful woman

338
00:19:03,843 --> 00:19:06,811
and clearly, your life works.

339
00:19:06,846 --> 00:19:09,213
There are others
not as fortunate,

340
00:19:09,248 --> 00:19:11,348
and without your inner strength,

341
00:19:11,383 --> 00:19:15,152
who would turn
to drugs or alcohol,

342
00:19:15,188 --> 00:19:17,988
to lives of self-destruction.

343
00:19:18,023 --> 00:19:20,925
Dennis was on that path.

344
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:24,662
As were many
others you see here.

345
00:19:24,697 --> 00:19:29,433
Most religions
claim to save souls.

346
00:19:29,468 --> 00:19:32,536
We also save lives, Miss Thomas.

347
00:19:34,673 --> 00:19:40,311
You must, you<i> must</i>
admire us for that.

348
00:19:51,524 --> 00:19:53,357
Hi. My name is Sarah.

349
00:19:53,392 --> 00:19:55,471
I have some information
I'd like to share with you

350
00:19:55,495 --> 00:19:56,775
that will change your life.

351
00:19:58,931 --> 00:20:00,798
Hi. I'm Sarah.

352
00:20:00,833 --> 00:20:02,600
Do you believe in the future?

353
00:20:02,635 --> 00:20:05,402
Can't be any worse
than my present.

354
00:20:05,437 --> 00:20:08,105
Believe me, the future is now,

355
00:20:08,140 --> 00:20:09,606
and you can be a part of it.

356
00:20:09,641 --> 00:20:11,242
Read this.

357
00:20:11,277 --> 00:20:14,111
And if you can, make
a small donation.

358
00:20:14,146 --> 00:20:15,846
Lady, I'm broke.

359
00:20:15,881 --> 00:20:18,226
I got laid off from my
job five months ago.

360
00:20:18,250 --> 00:20:20,094
Just got kicked out of my room.

361
00:20:21,454 --> 00:20:22,454
Hey!

362
00:20:38,837 --> 00:20:41,872
Run! Run!

363
00:20:41,908 --> 00:20:44,207
Let's get out of here.

364
00:20:45,577 --> 00:20:47,578
Go!

365
00:20:50,416 --> 00:20:52,427
Thank you. You all right?

366
00:20:52,451 --> 00:20:53,784
Yeah.

367
00:20:53,819 --> 00:20:55,452
Who were those guys?

368
00:20:55,487 --> 00:20:57,087
Deprogrammers.

369
00:20:57,122 --> 00:20:58,990
I live at the Future
Now Society.

370
00:20:59,025 --> 00:21:00,691
And what do they want with you?

371
00:21:00,726 --> 00:21:02,393
Parents do that.

372
00:21:02,428 --> 00:21:04,173
They don't want us to
be reborn in the future,

373
00:21:04,197 --> 00:21:06,277
so they hire
deprogrammers to go after us.

374
00:21:08,600 --> 00:21:10,178
You say you have
no place to live.

375
00:21:10,202 --> 00:21:11,435
Well, come to dinner.

376
00:21:25,050 --> 00:21:26,483
The Future Now Society

377
00:21:26,519 --> 00:21:29,320
will welcome your man
Tyler with open arms.

378
00:21:29,355 --> 00:21:31,689
I got to say, that
was a hell of a setup.

379
00:21:33,258 --> 00:21:36,159
I hope he can resist
their brainwashing.

380
00:21:36,195 --> 00:21:38,862
Well, I-I think he can.

381
00:21:38,897 --> 00:21:40,575
You know, given the
right circumstances,

382
00:21:40,599 --> 00:21:44,768
Tyler, you or me...
Brainwashing.

383
00:21:44,804 --> 00:21:46,737
It works.

384
00:21:54,547 --> 00:21:55,713
Wake, brother.

385
00:21:55,748 --> 00:21:57,848
The future is now.

386
00:21:57,883 --> 00:21:59,516
I just went to sleep.

387
00:21:59,552 --> 00:22:02,112
Rejoice, brother,
you were reborn.

388
00:22:09,762 --> 00:22:13,464
We are the future.
The future is now.

389
00:22:13,499 --> 00:22:18,035
We are the future.
The future is now.

390
00:22:18,070 --> 00:22:23,207
We are the future.
The future is now.

391
00:22:23,242 --> 00:22:26,977
We are the future.
The future is now.

392
00:22:38,291 --> 00:22:40,056
And now, just as
Joshua taught us,

393
00:22:40,092 --> 00:22:42,526
you will begin
your purification.

394
00:22:42,561 --> 00:22:45,462
You will undergo
four days of fasting,

395
00:22:45,497 --> 00:22:49,532
meditation, and the
fellowship of your brothers.

396
00:22:49,568 --> 00:22:51,202
You are the future, Tyler.

397
00:22:51,237 --> 00:22:54,004
Joshua loves you.

398
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:55,879
Joshua loves you.

399
00:23:19,264 --> 00:23:22,967
You have completed
your purification.

400
00:23:23,002 --> 00:23:25,035
Have you found
peace with us, brother?

401
00:23:25,071 --> 00:23:30,407
I've found peace,
I've found love.

402
00:23:30,442 --> 00:23:32,943
This is my home.

403
00:23:32,979 --> 00:23:35,178
We are the future.

404
00:23:42,888 --> 00:23:44,587
Still no word from Tyler.

405
00:23:44,623 --> 00:23:46,489
Well, give him time.

406
00:23:46,525 --> 00:23:49,293
Here's a message.

407
00:23:51,463 --> 00:23:54,731
Ben, Ben, this is Tyler.

408
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:56,110
Ben, where are you?

409
00:23:56,134 --> 00:23:57,501
He's in trouble.

410
00:23:57,536 --> 00:23:58,968
He sounded all right to me.

411
00:23:59,004 --> 00:24:00,904
Well, then why did
he hang up so fast?

412
00:24:00,939 --> 00:24:01,983
Well, probably
somebody was coming.

413
00:24:02,007 --> 00:24:03,240
He'll call back when he can.

414
00:24:03,275 --> 00:24:04,942
No, we've got to
go get him, Ben.

415
00:24:04,977 --> 00:24:06,221
Tyler can take care of himself.

416
00:24:06,245 --> 00:24:07,410
Most of the time,

417
00:24:07,446 --> 00:24:11,148
but he's undercover in
a cult with those people.

418
00:24:11,183 --> 00:24:13,284
What if they steal his mind?

419
00:24:16,688 --> 00:24:18,922
Huh.

420
00:24:18,958 --> 00:24:20,991
Ben!

421
00:24:21,026 --> 00:24:23,393
Patrick Morrison told me,

422
00:24:23,429 --> 00:24:25,862
the people most
vulnerable to cults

423
00:24:25,897 --> 00:24:28,632
are the ones who are
not happy with their lives.

424
00:24:28,667 --> 00:24:29,766
Tyler's happy.

425
00:24:29,801 --> 00:24:31,235
Oh, sure.

426
00:24:31,270 --> 00:24:32,714
He gets hit, kicked and shot at.

427
00:24:32,738 --> 00:24:35,072
The woman he dated for six
months eloped with his dentist.

428
00:24:35,107 --> 00:24:36,207
His rent was just raised,

429
00:24:36,242 --> 00:24:37,707
and he's being
audited by the IRS.

430
00:24:37,743 --> 00:24:39,409
Nothing's perfect.

431
00:24:39,445 --> 00:24:42,179
Ben! Just a little josh.

432
00:24:51,991 --> 00:24:54,091
Hi, Dennis. How's it going?

433
00:24:54,126 --> 00:24:55,437
Just fine, Tyler, and you?

434
00:24:55,461 --> 00:24:56,527
Great.

435
00:24:58,731 --> 00:25:00,697
Anna, what is it?

436
00:25:00,732 --> 00:25:02,666
Anna?

437
00:25:02,702 --> 00:25:04,935
I just can't believe
that Joshua is gone.

438
00:25:04,970 --> 00:25:08,639
How could this happen?

439
00:25:08,674 --> 00:25:10,607
Anna, what's wrong?

440
00:25:10,642 --> 00:25:14,044
I... I'm just... I'm just tired.

441
00:25:14,080 --> 00:25:16,746
I'm going to take
you up to your room.

442
00:25:16,782 --> 00:25:18,782
If anything
happened to the baby,

443
00:25:18,817 --> 00:25:21,051
Thomas would be very unhappy.

444
00:25:51,583 --> 00:25:55,519
♪ ♪

445
00:26:17,743 --> 00:26:20,022
Want to see his statements?

446
00:26:20,046 --> 00:26:22,606
Well, I'd like to
look at them myself.

447
00:26:25,384 --> 00:26:28,318
Tyler, what are you doing here?

448
00:26:28,353 --> 00:26:31,755
I was picking up
the dirty dishes.

449
00:26:31,790 --> 00:26:33,890
That's Anna's job.

450
00:26:33,925 --> 00:26:36,860
Oh, Anna isn't
feeling very well.

451
00:26:36,895 --> 00:26:39,128
The baby?

452
00:26:41,567 --> 00:26:44,101
Excuse me.

453
00:26:49,942 --> 00:26:51,086
Tyler!

454
00:26:51,110 --> 00:26:53,543
You're not getting
away with this.

455
00:26:53,578 --> 00:26:56,113
Wh-What?

456
00:26:56,148 --> 00:26:59,483
This sloppiness.

457
00:27:01,220 --> 00:27:04,287
You forgot the tray.

458
00:27:18,270 --> 00:27:21,371
Ah, Mr. Washburn.

459
00:27:23,709 --> 00:27:27,377
Well... nice.

460
00:27:29,281 --> 00:27:30,947
I asked the right people

461
00:27:30,982 --> 00:27:33,328
and found out you
keep an office in town.

462
00:27:33,352 --> 00:27:36,052
What do you want?

463
00:27:38,123 --> 00:27:42,926
Uh, well, before you joined
the Future Now Society,

464
00:27:42,961 --> 00:27:45,662
you were one of the most
successful corporate lawyers

465
00:27:45,698 --> 00:27:47,364
in Atlanta.

466
00:27:47,399 --> 00:27:49,099
Why'd you give it up?

467
00:27:49,134 --> 00:27:50,800
You wouldn't understand.

468
00:27:50,836 --> 00:27:52,001
I might.

469
00:27:54,573 --> 00:27:57,941
You're right, I was successful.

470
00:27:57,976 --> 00:28:00,611
I had the life we're
all taught to want.

471
00:28:00,646 --> 00:28:05,882
But I felt empty inside, hollow.

472
00:28:05,917 --> 00:28:10,254
So, I became what's
known as a seeker.

473
00:28:10,289 --> 00:28:11,922
I tried EST, Scientology,

474
00:28:11,957 --> 00:28:14,257
spent six months in
India with various gurus,

475
00:28:14,292 --> 00:28:15,258
but nothing clicked

476
00:28:15,293 --> 00:28:19,363
until I met Joshua Bradbury.

477
00:28:19,398 --> 00:28:25,435
From the moment I
met Josh, my life began.

478
00:28:25,471 --> 00:28:28,839
He was a true visionary,

479
00:28:28,874 --> 00:28:32,075
and the greatest
leader of our time.

480
00:28:32,110 --> 00:28:33,309
And very persuasive.

481
00:28:33,345 --> 00:28:34,611
The way I hear it,

482
00:28:34,646 --> 00:28:37,447
people were standing in
line to give him their money.

483
00:28:37,483 --> 00:28:40,484
And he put you at
the financial helm

484
00:28:40,519 --> 00:28:43,787
of this multi-million-dollar
enterprise.

485
00:28:43,822 --> 00:28:48,792
We are a way of
life, not an enterprise.

486
00:28:48,827 --> 00:28:50,739
Apparently, the federal
government disagrees.

487
00:28:50,763 --> 00:28:53,596
They're looking into
the Future Now Society's

488
00:28:53,632 --> 00:28:55,565
investments,
commercial properties,

489
00:28:55,600 --> 00:28:58,235
fishing fleets, travel agencies.

490
00:28:58,270 --> 00:29:02,005
The word is that you're about
to lose your tax exempt status.

491
00:29:02,040 --> 00:29:04,408
The federal government
has no business

492
00:29:04,443 --> 00:29:06,977
interfering with a
religious society.

493
00:29:07,012 --> 00:29:12,148
They can if they can prove
misappropriation of funds.

494
00:29:12,183 --> 00:29:14,418
Money diverted
to private accounts

495
00:29:14,453 --> 00:29:16,353
in, oh, Switzerland,
the Caymans.

496
00:29:16,388 --> 00:29:19,022
They'll never prove that.

497
00:29:19,057 --> 00:29:22,225
Especially with
Joshua Bradbury dead.

498
00:29:22,261 --> 00:29:24,828
You did know the
government was making a deal

499
00:29:24,863 --> 00:29:26,663
with your former leader?

500
00:29:26,698 --> 00:29:28,632
He was going to throw
you all to the wolves.

501
00:29:28,667 --> 00:29:30,133
What are you saying?

502
00:29:30,168 --> 00:29:33,504
That Joshua Bradbury's death
was a convenience for you.

503
00:29:33,539 --> 00:29:36,239
How dare you!

504
00:29:36,274 --> 00:29:39,209
The police told me that
he never dropped charges

505
00:29:39,244 --> 00:29:41,611
against an angry parent before.

506
00:29:41,646 --> 00:29:43,847
Who made the call
to drop the charges?

507
00:29:43,882 --> 00:29:45,348
I did.

508
00:29:45,383 --> 00:29:47,851
But it was Joshua's decision.

509
00:29:47,886 --> 00:29:50,620
It was in our best interests
to avoid bad publicity.

510
00:29:50,655 --> 00:29:52,567
And to make sure
that William Austin

511
00:29:52,591 --> 00:29:55,358
had no alibi.

512
00:29:55,393 --> 00:29:57,493
Did you make
the call that night?

513
00:29:57,529 --> 00:29:59,373
Did you make the
call to William Austin

514
00:29:59,397 --> 00:30:01,765
the night of the murder
about that fake meeting?

515
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:04,434
I did not.

516
00:30:04,469 --> 00:30:06,002
One of you did.

517
00:30:17,349 --> 00:30:18,793
Future, future, future,

518
00:30:18,817 --> 00:30:25,988
future, future, future,
future, future, future, future,

519
00:30:26,024 --> 00:30:29,893
future, future, future, future,

520
00:30:29,928 --> 00:30:32,229
future, future, future,

521
00:30:32,264 --> 00:30:36,700
future, future, future, future,

522
00:30:36,735 --> 00:30:40,037
future, future, future,

523
00:30:40,072 --> 00:30:43,874
future, future, future, future,

524
00:30:43,909 --> 00:30:46,310
future, future...
Killer! Killer!

525
00:30:46,345 --> 00:30:48,344
Killer! Anna, stop it.

526
00:30:48,380 --> 00:30:50,047
This is wrong.

527
00:30:50,082 --> 00:30:51,948
But he killed Joshua.

528
00:30:51,983 --> 00:30:54,617
As Joshua taught
us, this isn't the way.

529
00:30:54,652 --> 00:30:56,519
Don't worry, Anna,

530
00:30:56,555 --> 00:30:58,867
he'll pay for what he did.

531
00:30:58,891 --> 00:31:01,558
Martin Washburn told
me about your visit.

532
00:31:01,593 --> 00:31:04,060
He did?

533
00:31:04,096 --> 00:31:06,040
Your charges are more
than entirely unprovable...

534
00:31:06,064 --> 00:31:08,931
They're ridiculous, Mr. Matlock.

535
00:31:08,967 --> 00:31:11,267
I'm looking forward
to Dennis's testimony.

536
00:31:13,272 --> 00:31:16,273
Future, future,
future, future, future,

537
00:31:16,308 --> 00:31:20,077
future, future, future,
future, future, future...

538
00:31:20,112 --> 00:31:22,612
We've heard testimony

539
00:31:22,647 --> 00:31:24,592
that on the afternoon
Mr. Bradbury was murdered,

540
00:31:24,616 --> 00:31:26,283
your father threatened him.

541
00:31:26,318 --> 00:31:27,817
Is that true?

542
00:31:27,852 --> 00:31:29,920
Your Honor, we have
already stipulated

543
00:31:29,955 --> 00:31:32,322
that the defendant
threatened the deceased.

544
00:31:32,357 --> 00:31:33,590
Said he'd knock his head off

545
00:31:33,625 --> 00:31:34,758
and tried to strangle him.

546
00:31:34,793 --> 00:31:36,526
And I, for one, am proud of him.

547
00:31:36,561 --> 00:31:37,972
- Can we move on?
- Mr. Matlock!

548
00:31:37,996 --> 00:31:40,297
Proceed.

549
00:31:40,332 --> 00:31:44,034
On the night in
question, at 11:00,

550
00:31:44,069 --> 00:31:46,569
you were on your way
to Mr. Bradbury's study

551
00:31:46,605 --> 00:31:48,171
to bring him a cup of tea,

552
00:31:48,206 --> 00:31:51,341
is that right? Yes.

553
00:31:51,376 --> 00:31:55,711
Will you describe what happened?

554
00:31:55,747 --> 00:31:57,992
When I reached Joshua's study,

555
00:31:58,016 --> 00:32:02,152
I knocked on the door.

556
00:32:02,187 --> 00:32:04,154
I was about to enter...

557
00:32:06,158 --> 00:32:08,091
wh-when I heard...

558
00:32:11,096 --> 00:32:12,896
What did you hear?

559
00:32:12,931 --> 00:32:16,532
A gunshot.

560
00:32:16,568 --> 00:32:19,635
What happened next?

561
00:32:21,507 --> 00:32:25,809
I dropped the tray.

562
00:32:25,844 --> 00:32:28,545
I went into the room,

563
00:32:28,580 --> 00:32:32,649
and that's when I saw him...

564
00:32:32,685 --> 00:32:36,420
Joshua slumped over his desk,

565
00:32:36,455 --> 00:32:39,489
and I knew he was dead.

566
00:32:46,465 --> 00:32:49,198
You need a moment
to compose yourself?

567
00:32:57,743 --> 00:32:59,576
No.

568
00:32:59,611 --> 00:33:04,113
I'm fine.

569
00:33:04,149 --> 00:33:06,015
This testimony is my duty.

570
00:33:06,051 --> 00:33:08,885
My final service to Joshua.

571
00:33:08,921 --> 00:33:11,254
Proceed.

572
00:33:11,289 --> 00:33:13,890
You discovered
the decedent's body.

573
00:33:13,926 --> 00:33:15,825
What happened next?

574
00:33:15,861 --> 00:33:19,662
I heard a noise.

575
00:33:19,698 --> 00:33:21,230
When I looked up,

576
00:33:21,266 --> 00:33:23,377
I saw someone running
through the French doors.

577
00:33:23,401 --> 00:33:25,769
Did you recognize him?

578
00:33:25,804 --> 00:33:27,704
Not at first.

579
00:33:27,739 --> 00:33:30,184
But I ran after him.

580
00:33:30,208 --> 00:33:31,807
He ran through the gardens

581
00:33:31,843 --> 00:33:33,321
towards the trees
near the fence.

582
00:33:33,345 --> 00:33:34,477
I followed.

583
00:33:34,513 --> 00:33:37,447
Did this person have a gun?

584
00:33:37,482 --> 00:33:38,915
Yes.

585
00:33:38,951 --> 00:33:43,453
Dennis, when did
you recognize him?

586
00:33:43,488 --> 00:33:45,922
When he got near
the trees, he fell.

587
00:33:49,995 --> 00:33:54,130
<i>Then he turned his
face towards me.</i>

588
00:33:54,166 --> 00:33:56,799
<i>And I saw his face.</i>

589
00:34:01,239 --> 00:34:03,974
Dennis, whom did you see?

590
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:11,148
I saw him.

591
00:34:11,183 --> 00:34:13,116
William Austin.

592
00:34:22,827 --> 00:34:24,895
Thank you, Dennis.

593
00:34:24,930 --> 00:34:26,997
Nothing further, Your Honor.

594
00:34:27,032 --> 00:34:29,799
Cross-examine?

595
00:34:29,834 --> 00:34:32,102
No questions, Your Honor.

596
00:34:32,137 --> 00:34:33,603
No questions?

597
00:34:33,638 --> 00:34:35,249
What the hell do you
mean, no questions?

598
00:34:35,273 --> 00:34:36,673
Order in the court, please.

599
00:34:36,708 --> 00:34:38,675
He said in open court he saw me.

600
00:34:38,710 --> 00:34:40,310
You know damn well he didn't.

601
00:34:40,345 --> 00:34:42,912
It's no use.

602
00:34:42,948 --> 00:34:44,681
He believes what he's saying.

603
00:35:11,710 --> 00:35:13,688
Aren't you supposed
to be helping Anna

604
00:35:13,712 --> 00:35:15,690
in the kitchen, Tyler?

605
00:35:15,714 --> 00:35:17,325
I was looking for
some dirty dishes.

606
00:35:17,349 --> 00:35:20,283
Someone took my
papers from my desk.

607
00:35:20,318 --> 00:35:23,419
No? Not one of the brethren?

608
00:35:23,455 --> 00:35:25,032
We checked with
the phone company.

609
00:35:25,056 --> 00:35:27,235
You've been calling Mr. Matlock.

610
00:35:30,529 --> 00:35:35,432
I... don't live here anymore.

611
00:35:35,467 --> 00:35:37,787
Thomas, stop him!

612
00:35:50,849 --> 00:35:52,982
Look out!

613
00:35:53,018 --> 00:35:54,751
Hey, Tyler!

614
00:36:02,027 --> 00:36:05,261
I've gone over this transcript
of Dennis Austin's testimony

615
00:36:05,297 --> 00:36:08,998
so many times, I must, I
must be missing something.

616
00:36:09,033 --> 00:36:12,902
I can't look at it
again. It's so damning.

617
00:36:19,878 --> 00:36:21,778
Is it cold?

618
00:36:31,823 --> 00:36:35,592
I'm gonna see Patrick Morrison.

619
00:36:45,403 --> 00:36:48,071
<i>Mr. Oldham, how long</i>

620
00:36:48,106 --> 00:36:50,874
have you been a member
of the Future Now Society?

621
00:36:50,909 --> 00:36:52,687
For a little over five years.

622
00:36:52,711 --> 00:36:53,843
And during that period,

623
00:36:53,878 --> 00:36:56,312
you've risen to the
position of elder.

624
00:36:56,348 --> 00:36:58,725
Joshua chose me
as one of three, yes.

625
00:36:58,749 --> 00:37:02,418
So you would know everything
that goes on in this society?

626
00:37:02,454 --> 00:37:04,687
I would think so.

627
00:37:04,722 --> 00:37:06,689
Uh, including the government's

628
00:37:06,724 --> 00:37:09,892
investigation into
Joshua Bradbury's

629
00:37:09,927 --> 00:37:11,595
misappropriation of funds?

630
00:37:11,630 --> 00:37:14,063
Your Honor, I
object. This is another

631
00:37:14,098 --> 00:37:16,499
issue altogether and irrelevant.

632
00:37:16,534 --> 00:37:17,779
It is not irrelevant,
Your Honor.

633
00:37:17,803 --> 00:37:19,268
It goes to motive.

634
00:37:19,304 --> 00:37:22,238
Overruled. Proceed, Mr. Matlock.

635
00:37:22,273 --> 00:37:26,075
Now, Mr. Oldham,

636
00:37:26,111 --> 00:37:32,181
is it true that Joshua Bradbury
was being investigated

637
00:37:32,217 --> 00:37:35,652
by the federal government
for allegedly diverting funds

638
00:37:35,687 --> 00:37:38,954
to offshore banks, yes or no?

639
00:37:38,990 --> 00:37:40,290
Yes.

640
00:37:40,325 --> 00:37:46,095
Now, the night of the
murder, you say that you were

641
00:37:46,130 --> 00:37:47,864
uh, in your study.

642
00:37:47,899 --> 00:37:50,178
I was in meditation, yes.

643
00:37:50,202 --> 00:37:52,168
Are you sure?

644
00:37:52,204 --> 00:37:53,381
Objection:

645
00:37:53,405 --> 00:37:55,939
The question was
asked and answered.

646
00:37:55,974 --> 00:37:58,052
Sustained.

647
00:37:58,076 --> 00:38:01,577
Mr. Oldham, you're
in charge of the kitchen

648
00:38:01,613 --> 00:38:03,746
at the Future Now Society?

649
00:38:03,782 --> 00:38:06,949
The kitchen is part of
my responsibility, yes.

650
00:38:06,985 --> 00:38:11,487
A... a couple of days
after Joshua died,

651
00:38:11,522 --> 00:38:17,160
you told me every
night after dinner,

652
00:38:17,195 --> 00:38:22,665
he went to his study
and absolutely no one

653
00:38:22,700 --> 00:38:26,970
was permitted to
disturb him until 11:00

654
00:38:27,005 --> 00:38:29,339
when Dennis Austin brought
him his tea, is that right?

655
00:38:29,374 --> 00:38:30,485
Yes.

656
00:38:30,509 --> 00:38:34,344
Absolutely no one could
disturb Joshua Bradbury

657
00:38:34,379 --> 00:38:36,078
till 11:00 when tea was served?

658
00:38:36,114 --> 00:38:37,246
That's right.

659
00:38:37,282 --> 00:38:38,581
Answer me this:

660
00:38:38,616 --> 00:38:43,686
On the night he was
murdered, how did he get his tea

661
00:38:43,721 --> 00:38:45,788
before Dennis arrived?

662
00:38:45,823 --> 00:38:48,891
He didn't.

663
00:38:48,927 --> 00:38:50,560
He did, and I can prove it.

664
00:38:50,595 --> 00:38:53,395
Your Honor? It's
relevant, it's relevant!

665
00:38:53,431 --> 00:38:55,991
Mr. Matlock, proceed.

666
00:38:59,437 --> 00:39:06,309
Dennis told the police
in his statement to them

667
00:39:06,344 --> 00:39:09,312
that he went up to the
study, knocked on the door

668
00:39:09,347 --> 00:39:11,181
heard the shot and ran inside.

669
00:39:11,216 --> 00:39:16,486
But he testified in
this court yesterday

670
00:39:16,521 --> 00:39:19,889
that he went up to the
study, knocked on the door,

671
00:39:19,924 --> 00:39:23,626
heard the shot, dropped
the tea, then went inside.

672
00:39:23,661 --> 00:39:28,131
So I ask you again, how
did Joshua get his tea

673
00:39:28,166 --> 00:39:30,666
before he was murdered?

674
00:39:30,701 --> 00:39:33,770
He didn't.

675
00:39:33,805 --> 00:39:35,972
All right.

676
00:39:36,007 --> 00:39:37,673
What's this?

677
00:39:41,012 --> 00:39:44,714
This is a police photograph

678
00:39:44,749 --> 00:39:46,615
of the crime scene.
Now look at it.

679
00:39:46,651 --> 00:39:48,584
See if you see anything unusual.

680
00:39:48,619 --> 00:39:52,155
Anything unusual.

681
00:39:52,190 --> 00:39:54,523
Okay, look right there
at the edge of the desk.

682
00:39:54,559 --> 00:39:56,058
See that?

683
00:39:56,093 --> 00:40:01,764
That's a teacup. Now,

684
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:08,370
if Dennis dropped his
tea outside the door,

685
00:40:08,406 --> 00:40:10,272
how'd that tea get there?

686
00:40:10,308 --> 00:40:11,541
Well, how should I know?

687
00:40:11,576 --> 00:40:13,688
It was probably left
over from the afternoon.

688
00:40:13,712 --> 00:40:17,112
Oh, no, no, no. I spoke
with the medical examiner,

689
00:40:17,148 --> 00:40:21,083
and he said that Joshua
had several sips of tea in him

690
00:40:21,118 --> 00:40:23,720
before he was shot,
so I ask you again,

691
00:40:23,755 --> 00:40:25,521
where did this tea come from?

692
00:40:25,557 --> 00:40:27,489
How should I know?
You should know because

693
00:40:27,525 --> 00:40:30,159
you brought it just
before you shot him.

694
00:40:30,195 --> 00:40:31,694
That's not true.

695
00:40:31,729 --> 00:40:33,029
Yes, it is.

696
00:40:33,064 --> 00:40:40,837
When my client, Mr. Austin,
threatened Mr. Bradbury,

697
00:40:40,872 --> 00:40:45,407
you saw you had
your, your chance.

698
00:40:45,443 --> 00:40:48,377
You knew that Dennis
would be coming at 11:00.

699
00:40:48,412 --> 00:40:54,317
So you brought him his tea
a few minutes before 11:00.

700
00:40:54,352 --> 00:40:56,264
He probably asked you
what you were doing there,

701
00:40:56,288 --> 00:40:57,654
and you made up some excuse.

702
00:40:57,689 --> 00:41:00,657
But when Dennis knocked
on that door, you shot him.

703
00:41:00,692 --> 00:41:01,724
That's ridiculous.

704
00:41:01,760 --> 00:41:03,793
The man that Dennis
saw was his father.

705
00:41:03,828 --> 00:41:08,865
No! The man Dennis<i>
believed</i> he saw was his father.

706
00:41:08,900 --> 00:41:13,903
The question is, how could
Dennis see someone else fleeing

707
00:41:13,938 --> 00:41:17,507
the scene of the crime and
believe he saw his father?

708
00:41:17,542 --> 00:41:20,109
It's impossible.

709
00:41:20,144 --> 00:41:22,178
Really?

710
00:41:22,213 --> 00:41:27,283
I have spoken with
a foremost authority

711
00:41:27,318 --> 00:41:31,854
in the subject of brainwashing,

712
00:41:31,889 --> 00:41:33,956
and he not only
believes it's possible,

713
00:41:33,992 --> 00:41:37,660
he believes it's
exactly what happened.

714
00:41:39,330 --> 00:41:44,066
New recruits for the
Future Now Society.

715
00:41:44,102 --> 00:41:47,269
Are put through a
process which you called

716
00:41:47,305 --> 00:41:49,506
a "purification
process." Is that right?

717
00:41:49,541 --> 00:41:53,076
It's a spiritual process, yes.

718
00:41:53,111 --> 00:41:56,145
And for the duration
of this spiritual process,

719
00:41:56,180 --> 00:42:01,784
you don't allow them to
eat or sleep, is that right?

720
00:42:01,819 --> 00:42:05,254
They fast, they keep vigil, yes.

721
00:42:05,289 --> 00:42:08,391
And they learn to call all
non-members of the society

722
00:42:08,426 --> 00:42:10,226
by what name? Well... Answer.

723
00:42:10,261 --> 00:42:11,227
"Subversives."

724
00:42:11,262 --> 00:42:12,662
Subversives.

725
00:42:12,697 --> 00:42:18,368
So, you don't let them
sleep, you don't let them eat,

726
00:42:18,403 --> 00:42:22,305
and they believe that
all non-members are evil.

727
00:42:22,340 --> 00:42:27,009
So what you've done,
you break them down.

728
00:42:27,045 --> 00:42:30,646
You program their
minds, you brainwash them

729
00:42:30,681 --> 00:42:35,484
so that by the time, by the
time, these members have

730
00:42:35,520 --> 00:42:38,254
finished their
purification process,

731
00:42:38,289 --> 00:42:41,657
they think what you
want them to think

732
00:42:41,693 --> 00:42:44,027
and they see what
you want them to see.

733
00:42:44,062 --> 00:42:47,630
You don't understand. We
prepare them for a better world.

734
00:42:47,665 --> 00:42:54,236
Dennis Austin believed
he saw his father because

735
00:42:54,271 --> 00:42:56,405
that's what you
programmed him to see.

736
00:42:56,440 --> 00:42:59,242
Why would I kill
Joshua? I loved him.

737
00:42:59,277 --> 00:43:02,478
I believe you did.

738
00:43:02,514 --> 00:43:06,583
I believe you did.
He was your teacher.

739
00:43:06,618 --> 00:43:11,721
He preached lofty ideals:

740
00:43:11,756 --> 00:43:16,859
new life, new world, new values.

741
00:43:16,895 --> 00:43:19,962
But then he disillusioned you.

742
00:43:19,998 --> 00:43:27,003
Joshua, like so many
men in and out of public life,

743
00:43:27,038 --> 00:43:29,739
had a weakness.

744
00:43:29,774 --> 00:43:34,443
He found a soft woman
to be very appealing.

745
00:43:34,478 --> 00:43:36,913
He had an affair
with your wife Anna.

746
00:43:39,583 --> 00:43:41,984
Joshua would, would never
do such a despicable thing.

747
00:43:42,020 --> 00:43:45,588
You know, when
I, when I realized

748
00:43:45,623 --> 00:43:47,824
you were the one
who brought the tea,

749
00:43:47,859 --> 00:43:51,093
I had to find out everything
I could about you.

750
00:43:51,128 --> 00:43:53,796
So I went to see Patrick Morris.

751
00:43:53,831 --> 00:43:55,909
And what does he know about me?

752
00:43:55,933 --> 00:43:57,066
Not much.

753
00:43:57,101 --> 00:44:00,503
Not much, not much,
but he-he did suggest

754
00:44:00,538 --> 00:44:04,207
that I go see your
former wife Carrie.

755
00:44:04,242 --> 00:44:05,808
Pleasant woman, pleasant woman.

756
00:44:05,843 --> 00:44:09,312
She told me what she could
about the, about the, uh, cult,

757
00:44:09,347 --> 00:44:12,948
and she asked me about
your life now, and in passing,

758
00:44:12,983 --> 00:44:16,084
I told her that your
present wife Anna

759
00:44:16,120 --> 00:44:17,553
was gonna have a baby.

760
00:44:17,588 --> 00:44:21,390
Well, she was
shocked. You know why?

761
00:44:21,425 --> 00:44:24,794
Please don't do this.

762
00:44:24,829 --> 00:44:28,130
You and Carrie didn't
have any children, did you?

763
00:44:28,165 --> 00:44:29,198
No.

764
00:44:29,233 --> 00:44:33,568
You took those
tests to find out why.

765
00:44:33,604 --> 00:44:37,472
And those tests proved that

766
00:44:37,508 --> 00:44:40,342
yours was the
infertility problem,

767
00:44:40,377 --> 00:44:42,244
and it was uncorrectable.

768
00:44:42,279 --> 00:44:44,247
That right?

769
00:44:44,282 --> 00:44:47,950
And Anna, Anna didn't know that.

770
00:44:47,985 --> 00:44:50,719
So when she told
you she was pregnant,

771
00:44:50,755 --> 00:44:54,590
you knew you
were not the father.

772
00:44:54,625 --> 00:45:00,129
And you knew that Joshua
was the only other person

773
00:45:00,164 --> 00:45:01,497
she'd be that intimate with.

774
00:45:01,532 --> 00:45:02,631
That's a lie!

775
00:45:02,666 --> 00:45:04,299
You knew Joshua was the father,

776
00:45:04,335 --> 00:45:06,535
and that's why you killed him.

777
00:45:06,571 --> 00:45:08,070
Dennis, tell him it isn't true!

778
00:45:10,408 --> 00:45:17,546
Dennis knows his father
did not kill Joshua Bradbury.

779
00:45:17,581 --> 00:45:22,451
Dennis can remember...

780
00:45:22,487 --> 00:45:25,087
what he actually saw.

781
00:45:28,025 --> 00:45:32,194
Now he can look
back and remember.

782
00:45:53,284 --> 00:45:58,254
No. No!

783
00:45:58,289 --> 00:46:00,756
No, it was you!

784
00:46:03,861 --> 00:46:05,761
It was you!

785
00:46:24,081 --> 00:46:27,049
It's all over, son.

786
00:46:33,758 --> 00:46:35,502
Your Honor, in view
of the circumstances,

787
00:46:35,526 --> 00:46:37,471
the State moves to
dismiss all charges

788
00:46:37,495 --> 00:46:38,961
against William Austin.

789
00:46:38,996 --> 00:46:43,265
Case dismissed.
This court is adjourned.

790
00:46:45,770 --> 00:46:47,050
Thank you, Ben.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
